<mjml>
  <mj-head>
    <mj-font name="Source Sans Pro" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css?family=Source+Sans+Pro:200,400,700&display=swap" />

    <!-- defines the style for different tags -->
    <mj-style inline="inline">
      a {
        color: #fbc926; /* Make links this color */
      }
      p {
        margin: 0.2em 0; /* Adjusts vertical spacing */
      }
      h2 {
        text-decoration: underline; /* Adds underline */ margin-bottom: 0.1em; /* Adjust margin below */ color: #ffffff
      }
    </mj-style>
  </mj-head>

  <!-- defines the color of the background that the column of content sits on top of -->
  <mj-body background-color="#222">
    <!-- add an empty section for padding at the top of the email -->
    <mj-section> </mj-section>

    <!--  defines the background color behind the text -->
    <mj-section padding="0" background-color="#000000">
      <mj-column>
        <!-- insert a banner image -->
        <mj-image padding="0" width="600px" src="https://static.presidentscup.us/2025.11.18.game-of-the-month-banner.png" alt="2026 President's Cup Competition Banner. #PRESCUP" />

        <!-- defines the text style (font and color) -->
        <mj-text font-family="Source Sans Pro, sans-serif" padding-top="20px" font-size="16px" color="#ffffff" line-height="1.3">
          <!-- insert email content here -->
          <p>
            <span>Hello,</span>
          </p>
          </br>

          <p>
            <span>The President's Cup Cybersecurity Competition team challenges you to test your <b>digital forensics and secure software development</b> skills in this month’s </span>
            <span><a href="https://presidentscup.cisa.gov/game-of-the-month/">Game of the Month</a><b>: "Bravo Charlie Hotel"</b> (PC5, R2)!</span>
            <span>This challenge will encourage you to decrypt seized data, perform static media analysis, and strengthen your forensic expertise. </span>
          </p>
          <br />

          <p>
            <span>📌 <b>Work Role: </b><a href="https://niccs.cisa.gov/tools/nice-framework/work-role/digital-forensics">Digital Forensics (PD-WRL-002)</a></span><br />
            <span>📌 <b>Work Role: </b><a href="https://niccs.cisa.gov/tools/nice-framework/work-role/secure-software-development">Secure Software Development (DD-WRL-003) </a></span><br />
            <span>📌 <b>NICE Framework Tasks Covered: </b></span><br />
            <ul>
              <li><b>T1121</b>: Decrypt seized data</li>
              <li><b>T0179</b>: Perform static media analysis</li>
              <li><b>T1607</b>: Recover information from forensic data sources</li>
            </ul>
            <span>🔗 <b>Gameboard Link:</b> [<a href="https://pccc.cisa.gov/gb/practice/162d317b19a349d3a6ac441357f13308/bravo-charlie-hotel">Practice - Bravo Charlie Hotel</a>] 
          </p>
          <br />

          <p>
            <span><b>Why Participate?</b></span><br />
            <ul>
              <li><b>Develop Key Cybersecurity Skills</b> - Gain hands-on experience in digital forensics and software development.</li>
              <li><b>Boost Your Career </b> - Work on NICE framework tasks critical to cybersecurity investigations.</li>
              <li><b>Challenge Yourself </b> - Solve a real-world cyber incident scenario.</li>
            </ul>
          </p>
          <br />

          <p>
            <span>🔹 <b>Competition Stats:</b></span><br />
            <span>✅ <b>Solvability Rate</b>: 21%</span><br />
            <span>⏳ <b>Average Solve Time</b>: 94 minutes</span><br />
          </p>
          <br />

          <p>
            <span>Join the challenge today and put your expertise to the test! </span>
            <span>If you have any questions about the Game of the Month Challenge, please email the <a href="mailto:PresidentsCup <presidentscup@cisa.dhs.gov>">President's Cup Team</a>.</span>
          </p>
          <br />

          <p>
            <span>Federal employees looking to enhance their cyber skills can visit the <a href="https://pccc.cisa.gov/gb/practice">Practice Area</a> to tackle past PC challenges and earn completion certificates for continuing education credits.</span>
            <span>The <a href="https://github.com/cisagov/prescup-challenges">President's Cup GitHub</a> is another great way to access artifacts, solution guides, and additional resources from previous competitions.</span>
          </p>

        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- add an empty section for padding at the bottom of the email -->
    <mj-section> </mj-section>
  </mj-body>
</mjml>
